xnu-4903's LLDB macros are Python 2, so the build cannot finish on any
host whose `python` is Python 3.

The kernel compiles and links fine. What fails is the step after it: the
config_all pass that copies tools/lldbmacros into the kernel's dSYM bundle.
Every file is validated first by tools/lldbmacros/core/syntax_checker.py,
which is itself Python 2:

    print >>sys.stderr, "Error: Unknown arguments"
    print helpdoc

    SyntaxError: Missing parentheses in call to 'print'
    make[5]: *** [.../lldbmacros/zonetriage.py] Error 1
    make[2]: *** [config_all_recurse_into_tools] Error 2

Porting syntax_checker.py is not enough. Its actual job is

    py_compile.compile(fname, cfile="/dev/null", doraise=True)

on each file it is given, and the ~50 files under tools/lldbmacros are all
Python 2 as well. A Python 3 checker would simply reject every one of them
in turn. Making the whole directory run under Python 3 is the work Apple
itself only did several releases later, and none of it affects the kernel.

Drop the directory from the build instead. lldbmacros is a bundle of LLDB
commands for inspecting a live kernel over a KDP debugger connection -- it
is debugger-side tooling, not kernel code, and nothing in the kernel image
depends on it. The dSYM is still produced by dsymutil during the link; it
just carries no Python macros.

Deliberately not done: stubbing syntax_checker.py out to exit(0). That
would let the copy proceed and leave a dSYM holding macros that cannot
load, which is worse than a dSYM with none -- and it would silence the
check for anyone who later does port these files.

If you need the macros, port tools/lldbmacros to Python 3 and revert this;
nothing else has to change.

--- a/tools/Makefile
+++ b/tools/Makefile
@@ -6,7 +6,12 @@
 include $(MakeInc_cmd)
 include $(MakeInc_def)

-CONFIG_SUBDIRS = lldbmacros
+# lldbmacros is omitted: it is Python 2 and its own syntax_checker.py
+# py_compile()s every file, so the whole directory fails to install on a
+# host where `python` is Python 3. These are debugger-side LLDB commands
+# for a live KDP session; the kernel image does not depend on them, and
+# the dSYM is still produced by the link step without them.
+CONFIG_SUBDIRS =

 include $(MakeInc_rule)
 include $(MakeInc_dir)
